 just as important and that if  people she saves go on to defeat demons  it's her victory too because she is a  part of them now unfortunately i don't  see nosuke's parting words to ali here  if they did specifically feel the need  to exchange any after all inosuke is his  own beast who doesn't follow usual  conventions and while tundra and zains  are shown tearing up at their parting  with the butterfly estate girls inosuke  is just wearing his mask and we see no  tears you might think he might be crying  but just as a mask on but usually you  actually see tears coming through the  mask when he knows k cries still the  fact that ali uncharacteristically said  she enjoyed spending time with the trio  could be a sign that she liked having  inosuke around specifically too at this  point without knowledge of the future  it's definitely a stretch but knowing  what we know now it could be a clue  after the mugen train arc the gang is at  the butterfly estate again one day  tundra is returning from a solo mission  and this is when he overhears aoi  screams while tangent the sound hashira  is trying to forcefully take her on a  mission she looks very scared and  nervous she sweats as she tells the  hasha who is carrying her to let her go  he even tries to take one of the younger  girls at first who aren't even core  members and accordingly aren't wearing  the demon slang uniforms i briefly  mentioned this part with the sound  pillar near the beginning of the video  but it is really touching here that when  aoi screams out for kano's help kano  actually moves to do something it might  not seem like a big deal at first glance  but if you know her backstory you know  it's a super big deal she sweats a lot  as she thinks about her duty the fact  that tangent is a superior officer and  so on but then she recalls tundra's  advice to obey her heart and that gives  her the strength to grab hold of ali aoi  is brought to tears by the fact that  kano who for a long time just followed  the orders of superiors finally broke  that rule as far as the demonstrator  code goes it appears like tengen is in  his right to do this he implies that he  only needs to ask for shinobu's  permission to take a demonstra graduate  on a mission if she is atsuguko aka the  chosen successor of ahashira thus he  couldn't take khanau without asking  shinobu but he could take aoi official  demonstrator rules aside though everyone  else realizes how wrong he is from an  ethical standpoint and tundra steps in  to help he tries to headbutt tengen but  for once his super effective headbutt  misses because of tangent speed finally  tanjiro insists that if tangent needs  help he'll go instead of ali zainson  nosuke show up at this point and in  those cases before zanito and i quote i  just got back but i'm not tired i don't  mind going either end quote it's not  quite a proclamation of love but  whenever inosuke seems to be doing a  nice thing for someone else you gotta  stop and notice and in this case he does  it on his future wife's behalf their  feelings for each other aren't very  clear yet but the evidence that they  like each other and want to help each  other is slowly growing and it's  probably not lost on aoi here that  inosuke was willing to risk his life on  a dangerous mission to save her from  having to do so it's true that tundra  and zanitsu are willing to do so too but  they're already occupied with butting  love interests like kanou and nezuko now  let's fast forward to chapter 100 after  the trio come back from their upper moon  6 fight kano is by tunjura's side but  aoi isn't she comes in after tundra  wakes up crying because she blames  herself for all of their serious  injuries after all as she points out  they were hurt because they went instead  of her tundra finds out that tangent and  zanitsu's injuries weren't as bad as his  but when he asks about inosuke one of  the butterfly estate girls says he was  in danger for a while too she is not  crying at delivering this news but audi  is crying a lot it's actually quite the  touching panel she says i quote  inosuke's condition was really bad the  poison got deep in him so he was slow to  use breathing to stop the bleeding and  dot dot end quote she doesn't even  finish her sentence before tundra spots  inosuke on the roof this is a  significant moment where we finally get  aoi specifically worrying and crying  about inosuke we can assume that while  kano was by tundra's side the most aoi  was buyingosukes it's clear that no  other girl present had inosuke on her  mind and inner thoughts as much as aoi  did while inosuke calls himself immortal  and one of the little girls calls him  dumb it's aoi who steps in and holds  inosuke back from attacking her she  yells at him saying the poison doesn't  work well on inosuke but neither does  medicine so he has to be careful she  criticizes him for already forgetting  what shinobu told him but her outward  frustration clearly points to her caring  about inosuke after all she wouldn't get  so wound up if she didn't care about  what happened to him inosuke as  hilarious as usual tells aoi to shut up  and to stop pulling on him and even  calls her a shrimp only for her to say  that they aren't that different in  height it's a funny relationship dynamic  between two short-tempered loudmouths  with hearts of gold that's completely  different from the other romantic  relationship dynamics we see in the  series and even though they both act  like tsundere and haven't confessed  their feelings for each other after this  there is good reason to ship them  besides just the fact that the other  characters are already shipped with each  other aoi was deeply affected by his  injuries and continues to get emotional  about it even though he's fine now and  continues to care about him warning him  that he needs to be careful despite him  continuing to be rude to her as usual  and one can also assume that they  wouldn't care to bicker with each other  so much if they had no feelings for each  other it's been said that the opposite  of love is not hate but indifference and  these two are definitely not indifferent  with one another we also find out during  shinobu's fight against doma that aoi's  family was killed by demons just like  inosuke's mother was killed by a demon  namely doma it's significant that  inosuke helped defeat doma since it was  revenge for his mother but it was also  revenge for shinobu one of the most  important people in aoi's life now let's  fast forward to after the world is saved  from the demon king of pop inosuke and  aoi get another telling scene inosuke is  walking around the estate thinking about  how hungry he is he starts stealing food  while aoi is cooking and she calls him  out for it inosuke lies but wonders how  she notices so fast  and that maybe she's strong which is  definitely a plus in inosuke's books and  then we get an adorable part where aoi  gives inosuke his own plate and says  that when he's hungry he can eat from it  this plate will just be for him so he  can eat from it whenever he wants to the  implication is that she'll keep  refilling it and making special meals  for inosuke inosuke this time is the one  who stares at aoi and blushes he looks  down at the food and you see possibly  the cutest smile in the series plastered  on his face finally we have hard  evidence that inosuke is into aoi too  and that the way into his heart is  through his stomach then all that's left  is the confirmation that they end up  together and we get this in the form of  aoba hashibira the great grandson of  inosuke and aoi even before it was  officially confirmed that aoi was the  great grandmother it was suggested since  the allah in alba seem to come from the  awa in aoi then there's the new more  detailed ending they included in the  final demonstrator volume that gives us  some scenes that fill in some of the  gaps between chapter 204 and chapter  205. there's even o